---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — CG Design & Co."
  description="The terms that apply when you work with CG Design & Co. on a website project."
  pageTitle="Terms & Conditions"
  lastUpdated="12 November 2026"
>
  <h2>Who these terms apply to</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply whenever you ask CG Design &amp; Co. (ABN 25 672 082
    550) to design, build, or maintain a website or related work ("the
    services"). By agreeing to a quote or proposal from us, you accept
    these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Quotes and pricing</h2>
  <p>
    We give you a fixed, written price before any work begins, based on the
    pages and features you choose. That price won't change once agreed,
    unless you ask us to add extra pages or features partway through — in
    which case we'll agree the extra cost with you first. Figures shown by
    the pricing estimator on this site are indicative until confirmed in
    writing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our fee covers design and build only — it doesn't include the cost of
    registering or renewing your domain name. If we register a domain on
    your behalf, that cost is billed to you separately, at cost.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A 50% deposit is payable before work begins.</li>
    <li>The remaining 50% is due on completion, before the site goes live or files are handed over.</li>
    <li>Any ongoing care/hosting plan is billed on the 1st of every month.</li>
    <li>The hosting &amp; care plan includes up to 1 hour of content changes each month. Unused time doesn't roll over, and bigger changes are quoted before we start.</li>
    <li>Where we offer a free first month of the hosting &amp; care plan with a website package, billing starts from the following month.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we need from you</h2>
  <p>
    To keep your project on track, we need you to provide content (text,
    images, logos) and feedback within a reasonable time when we ask for
    it. Delays on your side may delay the delivery date.
  </p>

  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <p>
    Once the final payment has been made, the website and, if we registered
    it on your behalf, its domain name, belong entirely to you. Until then,
    the work remains our property. We may keep and display non-confidential
    parts of the finished site in our own portfolio unless you ask us not
    to.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel a project at any time by telling us in writing. You'll
    be charged for work already completed up to that point; any deposit
    already paid covering that work is non-refundable, and anything paid
    beyond work actually done will be returned. See our
    <a href={`${base}/refund-policy`}>Refund Policy</a>
    for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We'll do the work with reasonable skill and care, but we can't
    guarantee specific business outcomes (like a particular amount of
    traffic, bookings, or sales) from a website alone. We're not liable
    for losses caused by things outside our reasonable control — for
    example, outages at your hosting provider or a third-party service
    your site depends on. Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts, or
    modifies any consumer guarantee, right, or remedy you have under the
    Australian Consumer Law that cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of New South Wales, Australia,
    and any dispute will be handled in the courts there.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time; the date at the top shows
    when they last changed. Any project already agreed in writing is
    covered by the terms in place when you accepted your quote.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
